WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:05.513
This is one order, recorded start to finish on the live AgenticOrg service, with a

2
00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:10.757
test payment. A shop owner sets up a shop, a buyer's AI assistant finds it and

3
00:00:10.757 --> 00:00:15.933
builds the order, and the buyer pays the shop on the shop's own payment page.

4
00:00:17.919 --> 00:00:22.935
The merchant opens Sell everywhere and picks their new shop, Kaveri Coffee.

5
00:00:22.935 --> 00:00:28.353
They have already saved the keys of their own Plural account, in sandbox mode for

6
00:00:28.353 --> 00:00:29.356
this recording.

7
00:00:29.717 --> 00:00:34.543
The shop has no Shopify store, so it uploads a spreadsheet:

8
00:00:34.543 --> 00:00:37.406
two coffees, with prices and stock.

9
00:00:38.432 --> 00:00:43.871
Next come the policies buyers will see, and a flat shipping fee of forty-nine rupees

10
00:00:43.871 --> 00:00:45.425
for orders within India.

11
00:00:58.412 --> 00:01:01.909
Then the limits every AI agent must stay within:

12
00:01:01.909 --> 00:01:06.936
the largest order, the most per day, and the most items in one order.

13
00:01:06.936 --> 00:01:08.830
Nothing is set by default.

14
00:01:10.561 --> 00:01:16.042
For payment, AgenticOrg tests the merchant's Plural keys, and the merchant chooses

15
00:01:16.042 --> 00:01:18.983
to take payment in their own Plural account.

16
00:01:18.983 --> 00:01:21.724
AgenticOrg never holds the buyer's money.

17
00:01:22.091 --> 00:01:28.327
Last, the merchant names the shop on the network, accepts the terms, and turns Sell

18
00:01:28.327 --> 00:01:29.379
everywhere on.

19
00:01:32.227 --> 00:01:37.853
Turning it on enrols the shop with Grantex, which checks the catalog, prices and

20
00:01:37.853 --> 00:01:43.619
stock. AgenticOrg then publishes the shop's signed profile at its own web address.

21
00:01:47.385 --> 00:01:50.757
Shops on Shopify add their products another way.

22
00:01:50.757 --> 00:01:56.307
In the Shopify admin, they create an app that can read products and stock, then

23
00:01:56.307 --> 00:02:00.241
paste the store address and the app's access token here.

24
00:02:00.241 --> 00:02:04.666
AgenticOrg then reads the products, prices and stock by itself.

25
00:02:05.025 --> 00:02:10.679
Their buyers can also pay in the shop's own Shopify checkout, instead of Plural.

26
00:02:16.549 --> 00:02:22.408
A few minutes later, the web address has its certificate, and the shop is live.

27
00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:28.638
AI apps such as ChatGPT and Claude, the AgenticOrg bot on Telegram, and the open web

28
00:02:28.638 --> 00:02:33.013
can reach it, and buyers pay on the shop's own Plural page.

29
00:02:33.013 --> 00:02:36.795
Google, Microsoft and Perplexity are still to come.

30
00:02:38.694 --> 00:02:44.667
Now the buyer's side. A simple console stands in for the buyer's AI assistant, and

31
00:02:44.667 --> 00:02:47.726
makes the same live calls an AI app makes.

32
00:02:47.726 --> 00:02:52.606
The buyer wants two packs of filter coffee, delivered to Bengaluru.

33
00:02:54.396 --> 00:02:59.562
It lists the shops on the network and searches them, and finds the merchant's filter

34
00:02:59.562 --> 00:03:02.084
coffee at four hundred and twenty rupees.

35
00:03:02.546 --> 00:03:07.951
It opens a checkout for two packs, then adds the buyer's name and delivery address.

36
00:03:07.951 --> 00:03:13.161
The shop offers its flat shipping rate, and the total comes to eight hundred and

37
00:03:13.161 --> 00:03:14.398
eighty-nine rupees.

38
00:03:14.797 --> 00:03:18.584
The checkout is ready, so the agent asks to complete it.

39
00:03:18.584 --> 00:03:24.196
AgenticOrg checks the order against the merchant's limits and the verified catalog,

40
00:03:24.196 --> 00:03:29.065
records the decision, and returns a link to the merchant's payment page.

41
00:03:29.065 --> 00:03:31.228
The agent cannot pay on its own.

42
00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:39.039
The buyer opens the link. This is a Plural checkout under the merchant's own

43
00:03:39.039 --> 00:03:41.963
account, and the buyer pays with a test card.

44
00:04:23.077 --> 00:04:29.139
Plural sends the buyer back. AgenticOrg confirms the payment with Plural, and the

45
00:04:29.139 --> 00:04:30.560
order is confirmed.

46
00:04:39.324 --> 00:04:44.420
On the merchant's Orders page, the paid order appears with its items, the amount,

47
00:04:44.420 --> 00:04:49.580
and the delivery details the buyer gave. The merchant's administrators also get an

48
00:04:49.580 --> 00:04:52.096
email, and the merchant ships the order.

49
00:04:55.963 --> 00:04:59.368
That is the whole flow. The merchant set up once.

50
00:04:59.368 --> 00:05:05.135
A buyer's AI agent found the shop and built the order within the merchant's limits.

51
00:05:05.135 --> 00:05:07.983
And the buyer paid the merchant directly.

52
00:05:07.983 --> 00:05:11.110
The guides in this section explain each step.

